std::regex construction + regex_match over libstdc++ <regex>.
The former ADDRESS-LAYOUT-DEPENDENT symex abort is FIXED (system-header
bodies left with inconsistent returns are now demoted to the no-body
state).  Remaining issue: WHICH bodies half-convert still depends on
allocator address order; on most layouts the test verifies in
~91-300s, on some the extra havoc pushes BMC past practical time.
Root cause = an inner recovery swallowing a mid-body type-check
failure (RTTI branch of _Sp_counted_ptr_inplace::_M_get_deleter et
al.); fixing the swallow, or making resolution order canonical without
breaking first-wins consumers (cf. cpp17_std_function_lambda_call),
will make this flippable (2026-08-11).
